      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1810 the Virginia General Assembly authorized the Ashby’s Gap Turnpike, a toll road from Aldie to the Shenandoah River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.novaparks.com/parks/battle-of-upperville-goose-creek-historic-park/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Goose Creek Stone Bridge earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 1974.",
